0 0 0 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 55 766 Td (2. THEORY AND CONCEPTS) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 745 Td (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol \(DHCP\) automates host configuration. A client uses) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 730 Td (Discover, Offer, Request, and Acknowledgment \(DORA\) over UDP ports 68 \(client\) and 67) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 715 Td (\(server\). A scope/pool defines addresses and options such as subnet mask, default gateway,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 700 Td (and DNS. Addresses reserved for gateways and servers should be excluded. DHCP relay forwards) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 685 Td (requests across subnets because broadcasts are not routed by default.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 55 664 Td (Operating principles) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 643 Td (DHCP Server Implementation can be understood by following a communication from its source) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 628 Td (through the relevant interfaces and protocol layers. Each device processes only the) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 613 Td (information needed for its role. Correct operation depends on consistent addressing,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 598 Td (compatible link settings, correct service configuration, and a return path for replies.) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 577 Td (At the link layer, frames carry local delivery information such as source and destination) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 562 Td (MAC addresses. At the network layer, IP addresses and routing decisions identify the path) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 547 Td (between subnets. Transport and application protocols provide the end-to-end service when) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 532 Td (required. A failure at any layer can prevent the expected application behavior.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 55 511 Td (Important terms) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 490 Td (Key terms for this lab include dhcp server implementation, interface state, addressing,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 475 Td (forwarding, and verification. Distinguish configuration state from observed behavior: a) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 460 Td (command being accepted does not by itself prove that end-to-end communication works.) Tj ET
